# Experiment protocol: <name>

## Summary (after the run, for a person)

- **Result:** <!-- s --> <what was found, in at most two plain sentences that
  carry the question with them ("The class descriptions kept the cable set
  out of the framework class in all five cases") — the result, not the
  procedure; no intent ids, metric keys or run_ids, they are below>
- **Limits:** <!-- s --> <how far it holds, one sentence — the sample, a
  single run, what was not tested>
- **Next step:** <!-- s --> <what follows — a decision, the next experiment,
  or "none">
- **Question †:** <the question of the Intent in plain words — only where
  Result does not carry it>
- **Did †:** <what was done, one sentence — for a reader with no context>

## Intent (before the run)

- **Question / hypothesis:** <!-- s --> <the one question — what do we expect?>
- **Success / failure criterion:** <!-- s --> <how do we recognise whether it worked?
  One id per conjunct, written `[C…]` with its number in the brackets
  (C1 → the key `c1_pass`), each reappearing as a lowercase key in the reportable
  run's metrics.json (→ AS-003 Kein Lauf ohne Intent-Absatz, AS-004 Kennungen machen den Intent adressierbar)>
- **Admissibility condition:** <!-- s --> <what must hold in the same run before
  any verdict is issued — yield, coverage, a control showing its expected
  value; one A per condition; if one fails, there is no C verdict, only the
  finding that the instrument failed (→ AS-004 Kennungen machen den Intent adressierbar)>
- **Registered branch:** <if a result decides the conclusion or the next
  analysis, register it BEFORE the run: condition + what each branch
  licenses, one B per branch point (→ AS-013 Registrierte Weiche, AS-004 Kennungen machen den Intent adressierbar); "n/a" if there is
  only one outcome>
- **Timebox:** <hard budget, e.g. 4h — then log and ask>
- **Split touched:** <which split may be touched: train | dev | test>
- **Why this design †:** <choice of model, dataset, method — one sentence>
- **Rival explanations †:** <per confound: what OTHER than the hypothesis
  produces the same number · error direction (does it push for or against
  the hypothesis?) · the check as CODE in evaluate() (→ AS-044 Der Prüfblick auf einen Konfund ist Code)>
- **Out of scope †:** <the neighbouring questions this run leaves open>

## Result (after the run — write back, don't go quiet)

- **Answer to the question:** <!-- s --> <per registered id its verdict, and the
  run_id; numbers as a small table below the label (one row per arm or
  condition), produced by `analysis/<note>.py --check`, never retyped>
- **Raw output:** <!-- s --> <one real prompt+answer pair per finding>
- **Interpretation / next step:** <one sentence; keep instrument findings
  apart from findings about the subject>
- **Outcome †:** <expected or surprising — failures belong here>
- **Rival check †:** <which rivals are ruled out, which still stand?>
- **Caps/drops †:** <what was omitted or limited>
- **Analysis audit †:** <date · scope sha · N findings — the audit of the
  EVALUATION against the frozen criterion, before the number leaves; at
  cost seconds due at promotion or when the number steers a decision
  (→ AS-050 Auswertungs-Audit vor dem Berichten, AS-017 Die Zahl der Audits folgt der Kostenstufe)>

<!-- APPARATUS — this part gets LOOKED UP, not read. -->

## Context (self-contained)

- **Problem in one sentence:** <no technical terms — what is being found out?>
- **Terms of this protocol:** <!-- s --> <every name you coin, with a half-sentence a
  newcomer understands — constants (e.g. a margin), lanes or arms, item and
  case ids, the model alias, the files a reader meets; "n/a — standard
  vocabulary" only if the protocol coins nothing>
- **Prior threads:** <2–3 [[wikilinks]], each with half a sentence on why
  they lead here>

## Setup

- **Data / scope:** <!-- s --> <source, N, producer script; pilot subset first>
- **Model / tool:** <!-- sm --> <alias from `models.toml` — never hardcode endpoint/ID>
- **Prompt (verbatim, per variant):** <!-- sm -->

  ```text
  <the real prompt — `protocol-fill PROTOCOL-<name>.md --prompts` writes it from the script's PROMPT constants>
  ```

- **Model I/O:** <in: which fields · out as instructed: required format ·
  out in fact: what comes back + which function parses it>
- **Gate labels (expected) †:** <which labels the gate accepts — the declared
  set for the mechanical check against code-extracted labels>
- **Null condition / anchors (in the same run):** <!-- sm --> <one A per anchor — what runs along in THIS
  run and must show null — anchors of known rate, placebo (safest: one whose
  true answer is the same for every item), swap; not "was
  validated earlier". Per anchor its expected outcome WITH the derivation
  in half a sentence (→ AS-037 Jeder Anker trägt sein Soll mit Herleitung)>
- **Exclusions / filters:** <!-- s --> <what is dropped from the data or output and why;
  which outputs get no gate label — "none" if nothing is excluded>
- **Unit:** <!-- s --> <what one counted or judged thing is — and what is not:
  hidden files, nested directories, empty cases, a second answer line>
- **Data preparation †:** <raw → prepared: which script wrote which file;
  the experiment reads prepared only>
- **Meaning of the gold label †:** <what does the positive class REALLY
  mean? Check on the rendered example, not on the definition>
- **Answer form + resolution †:** <how many distinguishable states does the
  answer have, and where does the expected value sit?>
- **How measured †:** <metric or mechanism: what is compared, what counted>
- **Validation †:** <anchor items, second model or self-consistency, cross-check>
- **Noise ceiling → threshold †:** <measure repetition spread; the threshold
  comes from the null condition of THIS run>
- **Free knobs †:** <every preprocessing parameter with its value:
  thresholds, filters, cutoffs, windows>
- **Randomness controls †:** <seeds, number of runs, temperature setting
  and why — "deterministic" if no randomness>

## Checks (render check → instrument check → pilot)

- **Resolution check (ZERO calls, real `evaluate()` on synthetic
  extremes):** <perfect effect → criterion fires? · null effect → stays
  silent? Both numbers, with the run's real draw structure — computed by
  the actual evaluation code, never a hand copy of the formula; permanent
  form: `tests/test_<NN>_<name>.py`, run by `preflight` (→ AS-016 Auflösungsprobe vor dem Einfrieren)>
- **Render check (ZERO calls, `--show N`):** <per gold class ONE rendered
  prompt, read verbatim: stacked negation, fields inserted empty, sentences
  the question form cannot decide?>
- **Instrument check (real pipeline, ~10 calls, `--probe N`):** <per gold
  class ONE fully rendered prompt+answer pair as a code block, real data
  (→ AS-014 Je Gold-Klasse ein voll gerendertes Beispiel-Paar)>
- **Yield per stage:** <expected vs. obtained per parse step (→ AS-023 Kein stiller Verlust)>
- **Parser cases harvested:** <the probe's answer forms as REAL cases into
  the parser test — this is where they exist for the first time>
- **Clarified terms:** <what was ambiguous, and what is it called now?>
- **Changed — and in which class:** <instrument (wording, answer form,
  parser, field names) is allowed; hypothesis, criterion, admissibility condition are not
  (→ AS-008 Instrumentenprobe vor dem Einfrieren)>
- **Pilot:** <N items checked against hand analysis or anchors, before scaling>

## Runs (documented runs — via `runlog`, cite run_ids instead of retyping numbers)

- <run_id> — <one sentence: what this run was> <!-- s -->

